  "raw_note": "## VERIFIED FACTS\n\n### RAW Write Chain (Codex Analysis)\n**Call Path:**\n```\nFUN_0006887c (FAT Copier @ 0x6887c)\n  \u2193\nFUN_0006ccf8 (Image Handler @ 0x6ccf8)  \n  \u2193 @ 0x6d0f4 & 0x6d184\nFUN_00032500 (Alignment Wrapper @ 0x32500)\n  \u2193\nFUN_00094584 (RAW SD Transfer @ 0x94584)\n```\n\n**FUN_00032500** - Alignment enforcer:\n- Validates 0x200-byte (512) alignment\n- Converts: `start_lba = param1 >> 9` (bytes \u2192 sectors)\n- Converts: `sector_count = (len + 0x1FF) >> 9`\n- Calls FUN_00094584 with sector parameters\n\n**FUN_00094584** - Core RAW sector writer:\n- Parameters: `start_sector`, `sector_count`, `buffer_ptr`\n- Initializes SD slot via FUN_00051a64(0)\n- Programs SD controller MMIO registers directly (base 0xb0000000)\n- Sets LBA addressing (byte or block mode based on card type)\n- Executes multi-block transfer via controller registers\n- NO FatFS layer involvement - direct MMIO access\n\n### Critical Call Sites in FUN_0006ccf8\n**BOOT.bin write @ 0x6d0f4:**\n```c\nr0 = [sp+0x78] + 0x200   // Sector 1 offset!\nr1 = [sp+0x44]           // Length in bytes\nr2 = r7+0x20             // Buffer pointer\nbl FUN_00032500          // \u2192 RAW write\n```\n\n**APP.bin write @ 0x6d184:**\n```c\nr0 = [sp+0x78] + ???     // Likely 0x100000\nr1 = [sp+0x44]           \nr2 = r7+0x20\nbl FUN_00032500          // \u2192 RAW write\n```\n\n### NO CHECKSUMS / MINIMAL VALIDATION\n**From Finding-0021:**\n- FUN_0006ccf8 only checks: `bytes_read == file_size`\n- NO CRC32, NO MD5/SHA, NO signature verification\n- NO magic number validation beyond file existence\n- Bare minimum: file opens successfully + size matches\n\n**Security Impact:**\n- Corrupted files will brick device\n- No detection of truncated/modified binaries\n- User responsible for file integrity\n\n### Raw Binary Locations (Image Analysis)\n- **BOOT.bin**: Offset 0x200 (LBA 1), Size 12,736 bytes\n  - Signature: A5 5A 42 57 (ZBWp structure)\n  - ARM code @ 0x220\n  \n- **APP.bin**: Offset 0x100000 (LBA 0x800), Size 2,576,940 bytes  \n  - ARM IVT @ 0x100000\n  - Reset Vector: 0xEA000014\n\n### Single SD Card Architecture\n**CRITICAL CORRECTION:**\n- ONE physical SD card with multiple FAT partitions\n- Volume \"0:/\" and \"3:/\" are FAT partitions on SAME card\n- NO secondary SD card, NO internal flash in N9H26\n- Without SD card \u2192 IBR USB boot mode only\n\n**Partition Layout:**\n```\nSD Card (single physical):\n\u251c\u2500 Sector 0-2047:      Reserved Area (RAW binaries)\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500 Sector 1:        BOOT.bin @ 0x200\n\u2502  \u2514\u2500 Sector 2048:     APP.bin @ 0x100000\n\u251c\u2500 Sector 2048+:       Partition 0 = \"0:/\" (System/Working)\n\u2514\u2500 Sector X+:          Partition 3 = \"3:/\" (User/Update)\n```\n\n### Update Workflow (VERIFIED)\n1. User copies *.bin to \"3:/\" (update partition) via USB-MSC\n2. Device reboots, FUN_0006887c detects files on \"3:/\"\n3. **Staging phase:** FAT copy \"3:/\" \u2192 \"0:/\" (safety isolation)\n4. **RAW write phase:** FUN_0006ccf8 reads from \"0:/\" FAT, writes RAW via FUN_00032500\n5. Files deleted from \"3:/\" (prevents re-processing)\n6. Next boot loads from RAW sectors\n\n### Staging Area Rationale\n**Why copy 3:/ \u2192 0:/ before RAW write?**\n- Partition isolation: \"3:/\" = user space, \"0:/\" = system staging\n- Atomic workflow: If copy fails, RAW write never happens\n- State machine: Deletion of \"3:/\" signals \"update consumed\"\n- Protection: User cannot modify files during RAW write phase\n\n### Evidence Chain\n- Codex disassembly: Complete RAW write chain with addresses\n- TestDisk: Deleted FAT entries match RAW binary sizes exactly\n- Image analysis: Binaries at 0x200 and 0x100000 confirmed\n- No validation code found in FUN_0006ccf8 beyond size check\n\n## RELATED FINDINGS\n- Finding-0020: Volume management (\"0:/\" and \"3:/\" partitions)\n- Finding-0021: APP load mechanism confirms \"no checksum\"\n- Finding-0013: USB trigger may initiate update detection",
